This repository is public so you can learn from it. Read it, run it, take it apart, and
use what you learn to make something of your own. Please don't copy the portfolio itself.

You may:

1. Read, run and study the source.
2. Reuse techniques and pieces of the code, such as a function, a shader routine or a
   component, in projects with their own design and content. Where you do, keep a link
   to https://github.com/hyamero/portfolio in your source.
3. Make your own variations on its ideas: your own sky, layout, type and identity.

You may not:

1. Publish this site, or a version substantially the same in look and content, as your
   portfolio or anyone else's.
2. Use my name, likeness, writing, résumé or images, or the hyamero name and mark.
3. Reuse the site's design as a whole: its sky, layout, type and colours together.

If this site inspired yours, a mention is welcome but not required. For anything not
covered here, ask me at daleban.dev@gmail.com. Everything not granted above is reserved.

